{
  "name": "merge-state-refs",
  "description": "S2c and S2d. A state Value with page scope gets the prefix on its key wherever it sits in props: alone, as a transform input, in a transform's `by` and template `params`, in a conditional's `when`, `then` and `else`, inside a map or a list, in a nested SubPage's `pageId` and `params`. A dotted key is prefixed as a whole. App-scoped references are left alone. The same holds in the `map`, `filter` and `contains` transforms and the `contains`, `startsWith`, `matches` and `or` conditions. A reference with no `scope` is page-scoped. A static Value is data and is never rewritten, with or without a `value`, and gives no watch. `watches` carries bare keys with no scope, so an entry is prefixed when the node's props hold a page-scoped reference with that key; a key read in both scopes is listed twice, prefixed then bare.",
